From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:36:43 -0500
Subject: feat: the address row only on hover while the sidebar is closed
 (S-542)

GitHub issue 120, the owner's choice of 2026-11-16 (PLAN.md decision 24).
"Show the address row only on hover", in Settings > Stedding > Sidebar
and the command bar, off by default (stedding.toolbar.hide_in_compact;
toolbar T64, settings T75). With it on, a window whose sidebar is closed,
to the rail or hidden, hides its address row and the bookmarks bar under
it, and the page takes the window's top. On Windows the caption buttons
the row held go to the window's top corner over the page, the corner of
sidebar Y54, so the row no longer stays for them (T22).

The pointer resting at the window's top edge brings the row in over the
page, as a hidden sidebar comes in from the window's side: the page does
not move, and the row slides down over it on a layer of its own, drawn
over the page, with its ground and the page's colour painted by the top
container. The edge and the rest are the ones a hidden sidebar has at the
window's right edge, from the same settings (a sixth of the edge, 2 DIP
at the least; the rest and 200 ms more), because a page's own controls
sit along its top as its scroll bar sits at the right. The row stays
while the pointer is on it or the keyboard focus is in it, and slides
away when the pointer leaves for the page; on Windows the window's
buttons come and go with it. The window lays out twice while the row is
in: the page as with the row hidden, the row as with it shown.

A localhost page and Shift-Cmd-D keep the row as before. Full screen,
popups, little windows and apps' windows keep their own rules. The find
bar hangs under the row while it is in. The keyboard's command to move
the focus to the toolbar brings it in at once.

Why: GitHub issue 120 asked for compact mode to hide the title bar too;
the owner chose it for 0.6.0 on 2026-11-16.
Removable when: never as behaviour.
